  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member, I want the account button at the **top left**, as in legacy, and the **same button on every main screen**: Catégories, Favoris, Messages, Recherche and Plus. Then I always find my accounts in the same place. (Operator feedback, 2026-11-17, device screenshot: today the button sits top right, and only on some screens.) Parity and consistency.\n\n### Legacy @ 87fe0d1c\n\n- `HFRswift/Swift/MainToolbar.swift:59-65` (`MainToolbarContent`): `ToolbarItemGroup(placement: .navigationBarLeading) { Menu { menuItems() } label: { ToolbarProfileImage(image: profileImage, url: profileImageURL) } }`. The account menu is **leading**, and its label is the **account's avatar** (`ToolbarProfileImage`). The rows come from `AccountMenuViews.swift` (`AccountMenuRow`, `AccountAvatarView`, with a `person.crop.circle` fallback).\n- `MainToolbarContent` is used by `Favorites.swift:799` and `MPListView.swift:669`. `MainWindow.swift:260-282, 945-968` build the same account menu items for the other roots. Read them to list the screens legacy covers, and cite the lines in the spec.\n\n### Today (dev-swift)\n\n`App/SwiftHFR/Accounts/AccountMenuButton.swift` sits at `.primaryAction`, which is trailing on iPhone:\n- `Navigation/ForumListView.swift:29-30` (Catégories);\n- `Root/PlusView.swift:32`;\n- `Root/RootSidebarView.swift:57`.\n\nIt is missing from Favoris, Messages and Recherche (check each).\n\n### Scope\n\n1. Move the account button to the **leading** position (`.topBarLeading`) on the five main tab roots: Catégories, Favoris, Messages, Recherche and Plus. Also the iPad sidebar root, keeping it leading there.\n2. **Label:** the current account's avatar when it is known, as in legacy's `ToolbarProfileImage`, with the person symbol as fallback. Keep the expired badge (`person.crop.circle.badge.exclamationmark`).\n3. Pushed screens (a topic list, the reader) do not get it, because the back button is leading there. Say whether legacy does the same.\n4. No overlap with the large title, the title pill (#1012) or the trailing buttons (refresh, `…`). Check the Duo cover screen and its bottom-bar refresh placement (`refreshToolbarPlacement`).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- A view test (or an `ImageRenderer`/accessibility test) on each of the five roots: the account item is present and leading.\n- The legacy pointer comment on the modified views (AGENTS.md §4).\n- A `### Ledger` `changelog` entry: a parity fix citing `MainToolbar.swift:59-65`.\n- Tests fail without the change.\n\n### Device check (for the #893 general review)\n\nThe account button is top left on all five tabs, with the avatar shown.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
